  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"1a\"><p><strong>1a</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Impulse is change in momentum.</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"1b\"><p><strong>1b</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>The area under the graph <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"= \\Delta p = \\frac{1}{2}(10 \\times 10^{-3})(350) = 1.75\"></span> N s</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.75 = (0.046)v\"></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v = 38 \\approx 40\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span></p>\n<p>Calculated answer must be given to at least 2 significant figures in order to earn the final mark.</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"1c\"><p><strong>1c</strong></p><p></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{ave} = \\frac{\\Delta p}{\\Delta t} = \\frac{1.75}{10 \\times 10^{-3}} = 175\"></span> N</p>\n<p></p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The graph shows how the horizontal force exerted by a golf club on a golf ball varies with time. The mass of the golf ball is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"46\"></span> grams. The golf ball is initially at rest.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>a. Define impulse.</p>\n<p>   [1]</p>\n<p>b. Show that the speed of the golf ball as it loses contact with the golf club is about <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"40\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span>. </p>\n<p>   [3]</p>\n<p>c. Calculate the average force exerted by the golf club on the golf ball.</p>\n<p>   [1]</p>"
  },
